t/answer.txt` before the final chat response only after the\n  requested quantity has been computed successfully.\n- `codex_output/answer.txt` — exactly one line, canonical answer only. No\n  labels, prose, Markdown, alternatives, citations, units labels, or caveats.\n  - Numbers: decimal or scientific notation, no thousands separators.\n  - Percentages: value + `%` only when the question asks for a percentage.\n  - Strings/genes/chromosomes: exact label only.\n  - Direction/category/choice answers: exact requested label only.\n\nA failed command or package is not evidence that the benchmark item has no\nsolution. Continue with a valid repair or alternate execution route within the\nactive runtime limits. If execution still fails, do not guess and do not write\n`answer.txt`.\n--- task\n{\n  \"tag\": \"bixbench\",\n  \"version\": \"1.5\",\n  \"question\": \"In a bacterial swarming assay compared mixed cultures of Strain 287 and Strain 98 at various ratios, which ratio produced colonies with a mean area and circularity value that is most similar to the mean area and circularity values observed in Strain 1?\",\n  \"categories\": \"Imaging\",\n  \"source\": \"BixBench-Verified-50\",\n  \"ground_truth_visible\": false\n}\n--- manifest\n{\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Swarm_2.csv\",\n      \"workspace_path\": \"inputs/Swarm_2.csv\",\n      \"size_bytes\": 1620,\n      \"sha256\": \"c85fbaa900c3db64d55ffb81421267e68e5c43d7d37d90a767328c6e63522475\",\n      \"staging_mode\": \"hardlink\",\n      \"source\": \"staged_capsule_data\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pandas as pd, numpy as np\np='/workspace/inputs/Swarm_2.csv'\ndf=pd.read_csv(p)\nprint(df.dtypes)\nprint(df.groupby(['StrainNumber','Ratio'])[['Area','Circularity']].mean())\n# distances raw, standardized across all groups, standardized across mixed groups, min-max scaling etc\nstrain1=df[df.StrainNumber==1][['Area','Circularity']].mean()\nmixed=df[df.StrainNumber=='287_98']\nprint('strain1', strain1)\n# scale using all data including strain1\nfor label, subset in [('all', df), ('mixed', mixed)]:\n    means=subset.groupby('Ratio')[['Area','Circularity']].mean()\n    X=means\n    # zscore over ratio means\n    zmu=X.mean(); zsd=X.std(ddof=0)\n    z=(X-zmu)/zsd\n    ztarget=(strain1-zmu)/zsd\n    dist=(z-ztarget).pow(2).sum(1).pow(.5)\n    print('\\\\n', label, 'zscore ratio means')\n    print(pd.DataFrame({'dist':dist,'zarea':z.Area,'zcirc':z.Circularity}).sort_values('dist'))\n    # zscore over individual observations\n    obs=subset[['Area','Circularity']]\n    omu=obs.mean(); osd=obs.std(ddof=0)\n    zg=(X-omu)/osd; zt=(strain1-omu)/osd\n    dist2=(zg-zt).pow(2).sum(1).pow(.5)\n    print('zscore obs')\n    print(pd.DataFrame({'dist':dist2,'zarea':zg.Area,'zcirc':zg.Circularity}).sort_values('dist'))\n    # feature range minmax using individual obs\n    omin=obs.min(); omax=obs.max()\n    norm=(X-omin)/(omax-omin); nt=(strain1-omin)/(omax-omin)\n    dist3=(norm-nt).pow(2).sum(1).pow(.5)\n    print('minmax obs')\n    print(pd.DataFrame({'dist':dist3,'a':norm.Area,'c':norm.Circularity}).sort_values('dist'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
